# Kivo runs with ZERO configuration — this file documents optional extras.
# Copy to .env if you want any of them.

# ── Optional: AI surfaces ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kivo ships with no bundled AI provider. Without these variables the two
# AI surfaces (grounded Q&A in the reader, plain-language rewrite in the
# reading-level panel) abstain honestly; every other feature works.
#
# To enable them, point the app at ANY OpenAI-compatible chat-completions
# endpoint — OpenAI, Groq, Together, Mistral, DeepSeek, OpenRouter, or a
# local Ollama / llama.cpp server:
#
#   LLM_API_KEY=sk-...                # required to switch AI on
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1   # any OpenAI-compatible base
#   LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini             # any chat model the endpoint serves
#
# Example for a local Ollama (no cloud, no cost):
#   LLM_API_KEY=ollama
#   LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_BASE_URL / OPENAI_MODEL are accepted as aliases.

# ── Optional: Semantic Scholar (higher rate limits) ───────────────────
# Search and the citation map work without a key (shared public pool).
# A free API key lifts the rate limit:
#   https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api
# SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: key-gated academic providers ────────────────────────────
# Crossref, arXiv and Europe PMC are always on. These need keys:
#   CORE_API_KEY=          # https://core.ac.uk/services/api
#   IEEE_API_KEY=          # IEEE Xplore MetaProxy
#   OPENALEX_API_KEY=      # https://docs.openalex.org/
#
# Polite-pool mailto for Crossref and OpenAlex (recommended):
#   ACADEMIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=you@your-domain.example
